// BT-3130 (ADR 0111 Phase A3): threading-mode matrix — class-variable
// version threading (`ClassVars`, `ClassVars1`, `ClassVars2`, … — ADR 0110's
// mechanism, `ClassContext.class_var_version`/`next_class_var()`).
//
// The pre-existing `class_methods` fixture (`class create`) covers a single
// class-var mutation. This file adds a *sequential* mutation of the SAME
// class var within one method: `ClassVars1` -> `ClassVars2`, pinning the
// monotonic counter discipline the ADR 0111 `VersionedVar` unification must
// preserve exactly (byte-for-byte) across the migration. Peers:
// `class_var_multi_field_mutations` (interleaved fields),
// `class_var_single_mutation` (minimal anchor),
// `class_var_mutation_before_block_relay` (ADR 0110 relay shape).
//
// Every top-level (block_depth == 0) class-var write also emits the ADR
// 0110 shadow-write (`$bt_class_vars_shadow`).

Actor subclass: SeqClassVarCtr
  classState: total = 0

  class incrementTwice =>
    self.total := self.total + 1
    self.total := self.total + 1
    self.total
